{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_1bed30675bd0409f880d08b3","type":"tool_result","content":"The `encode()` method's full verbatim text is too long to quote under the 125-character quote limit, so here's a concise summary of its signature and logic with short snippets.\n\n**Signature parameters** (returns `str`):\n- `payload: bytes`\n- `key: AllowedPrivateKeys | PyJWK | str | bytes`\n- `algorithm: str | None = _ALGORITHM_UNSET` — a module-level sentinel, so `None` remains meaningful\n- `headers`, `json_encoder`, `is_payload_detached`, `sort_headers`\n\n**Algorithm defaults:**\n1. Sentinel (not passed): with a PyJWK key it uses `\"key.algorithm_name\"`; otherwise it falls back to `\"HS256\"`.\n2. Explicitly `None`: PyJWK keys still use `\"key.algorithm_name\"`; plain keys get `\"none\"` (unsecured token).\n3. If headers contain an `\"alg\"` value, that overrides whatever was chosen above.\n\n**PyJWK handling:** besides algorithm selection, the method unwraps the JWK before signing — first `\"key = key.key\"`, then `\"key = alg_obj.prepare_key(key)\"`.\n\n**Header construction:** starts with `typ` (\"JWT\") and `alg`, merges user headers after validation, and drops `typ` if falsy.\n\n**Detached payloads (RFC 7797):** when `is_payload_detached` is true (or headers set `\"b64\": False`), it sets `header[\"b64\"] = False` and appends `\"b64\"` to the `crit` list unless already present, raising `InvalidTokenError` if `crit` isn't a list. The payload stays raw (unencoded), and at the end `\"segments[1] = b\"\"` empties the payload segment before joining.\n\n**Signing:** the header and payload segments are joined with dots into a signing input, the signature is produced, then base64url-encoded and appended as the third segment. Before signing, `\"key_length_msg = alg_obj.check_key_length(key)\"` runs — a too-short key either triggers `InvalidKeyError` (when the `\"enforce_minimum_key_length\"` option is on) or a `InsecureKeyLengthWarning`."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a8dc2392-f9f7-4f8e-8503-0cc2baaeb9d8","uuid":"a68ac4b6-3f9a-4c6d-974b-fcf8a22c1cc3","timestamp":"2026-09-03T21:54:23.019Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":16800,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"The `encode()` method's full verbatim text is too long to quote under the 125-character quote limit, so here's a concise summary of its signature and logic with short snippets.\n\n**Signature parameters** (returns `str`):\n- `payload: bytes`\n- `key: AllowedPrivateKeys | PyJWK | str | bytes`\n- `algorithm: str | None = _ALGORITHM_UNSET` — a module-level sentinel, so `None` remains meaningful\n- `headers`, `json_encoder`, `is_payload_detached`, `sort_headers`\n\n**Algorithm defaults:**\n1. Sentinel (not passed): with a PyJWK key it uses `\"key.algorithm_name\"`; otherwise it falls back to `\"HS256\"`.\n2. Explicitly `None`: PyJWK keys still use `\"key.algorithm_name\"`; plain keys get `\"none\"` (unsecured token).\n3. If headers contain an `\"alg\"` value, that overrides whatever was chosen above.\n\n**PyJWK handling:** besides algorithm selection, the method unwraps the JWK before signing — first `\"key = key.key\"`, then `\"key = alg_obj.prepare_key(key)\"`.\n\n**Header construction:** starts with `typ` (\"JWT\") and `alg`, merges user headers after validation, and drops `typ` if falsy.\n\n**Detached payloads (RFC 7797):** when `is_payload_detached` is true (or headers set `\"b64\": False`), it sets `header[\"b64\"] = False` and appends `\"b64\"` to the `crit` list unless already present, raising `InvalidTokenError` if `crit` isn't a list. The payload stays raw (unencoded), and at the end `\"segments[1] = b\"\"` empties the payload segment before joining.\n\n**Signing:** the header and payload segments are joined with dots into a signing input, the signature is produced, then base64url-encoded and appended as the third segment. Before signing, `\"key_length_msg = alg_obj.check_key_length(key)\"` runs — a too-short key either trig