{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"gen-1788472687-Lta9sIHms5P3jiK1y6gV","type":"message","role":"assistant","container":null,"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. JWKs are now supported for both JWS and JWT encoding, with automatic algorithm selection.\n\n## Changes\n\n**`jwt/api_jws.py`** (`jwt/api_jws.py:105-170`)\n- `encode()` now accepts `PyJWK` objects: `key: AllowedPrivateKeys | PyJWK | str | bytes`\n- `algorithm` is now optional (`None` default) instead of hardcoding `\"HS256\"`\n- Algorithm resolution: if `algorithm` is `None`, a `PyJWK` key yields `key.algorithm_name`, while any other key type falls back to `\"HS256\"`; an explicit `algorithm` argument always wins (and `headers={\"alg\": ...}` still takes precedence over both)\n- Before signing, a `PyJWK` is unwrapped to its prepared key material (`key.key`) before `alg_obj.prepare_key()` runs\n\n**`jwt/api_jwt.py`** (`jwt/api_jwt.py:45-49`)\n- Same signature update; `PyJWT.encode()` delegates to `api_jws.encode()`, so the resolution logic applies identically to JWTs\n\n**`tests/test_api_jws.py`**\n- Added `test_encode_default_algorithm` and `test_encode_with_jwk` (an `oct`/HS256 JWK round-trips with identical signature bytes to the string-key token)\n- Updated two tests that previously used `algorithm=None` to request unsecured tokens to pass `algorithm=\"none\"` explicitly — `None` now means \"choose from the key\", not \"no algorithm\"\n\n**`CHANGELOG.rst`** — added an entry under Unreleased → Changed.\n\n## Verified\n\n- Full suite: **273 passed, 4 skipped, 1 xfailed** (the skips are `no_crypto_required` tests that only run without `cryptography`, which is installed here)\n- Functional checks: JWS+JWK and JWT+JWK round-trips (both `oct`/HS256 and `EC`/ES256), raw-key defaulting to HS256, explicit-algorithm override, header `alg` override, and `algorithm=\"none\"` all behave correctly\n\nOne behavioral note worth knowing: `encode(payload, key=None)` previously produced an unsecured `alg: \"none\"` token; it now attempts HS256 and fails. Creating unsecured tokens still works, but requires `algorithm=\"none\"` explicitly — this matches the upstream design and removes an easy footgun.","citations":[]}],"model":"z-ai/glm-5.3-flash","stop_reason":null,"stop_details":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_details":null,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"inference_geo":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null,"speed":"standard"},"provider":"Z.AI","context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a8dc2392-f9f7-4f8e-8503-0cc2baaeb9d8","uuid":"8fd0096e-c6d1-4bfb-a6a4-bf7c6de538a1","timestamp":"2026-09-03T21:58:23.712Z","request_id":"gen-1788472687-Lta9sIHms5P3jiK1y6gV"}
